WMBlueCPU - a dockapp

	WMBlueCPU shows system cpu usage. It runs as a dockapp for
WindowMaker or some other window manager which supports dockapps.
	The following options can be passed to WMBlueCPU on the command
line:
	-h, --help             - Display basic usage info and exit
	-v, --version          - Display version and exit
	-display <DISPLAY>     - The X11 display to connect to
	-m <MILISECS>          - The number of miliseconds between updates
	-w,  --window          - Run in a window
	-nw, --no-window       - Don't run in a window
	-s,  --shape           - Use the XShape extension
	-ns, --no-shape        - Don't use the XShape extension, create own panel.

